Enhancement: Let the server assemble large uploads in the background

After the last chunk of a large file the client kept a single request open
until the server had assembled the file. For files of several gigabytes this
takes minutes, and proxies in front of the server cut the connection before the
answer arrived: the upload was reported as failed although the file was
complete on the server, and it was uploaded again.

For files of 100 MB and more the client now asks the server to assemble the
file in the background (header OC-LazyOps on the final MOVE) and polls the
result: after 0.5, 1, 2 and 4 seconds, then every 5 seconds. Servers that do
not offer this ignore the header and answer as before. A database deadlock
reported for the assembly is retried like before, other errors are handled
like the errors of a direct answer. The environment variable
OWNCLOUD_ASYNC_FINALIZE_MIN_SIZE changes the size limit; a negative value
turns the behaviour off.
